{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/302861-adapting-monsters-for-use-in-geist","id":302861,"title":"Adapting monsters for use in Geist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-04T19:31:16-08:00","id":302861,"title":"Adapting monsters for use in Geist","content":"I'm considering monsters and obstacles for use in a Geist game - particularly, Dread powers from Hunter books seem like an excellent way to build enemies to throw at my players, and make much simpler stat blocks should I wish to throw a witch, mummy or demon at them. Has anyone else taken this approach? Power level wise, can anyone offer me a way to make sure monster power levels are in the right ball park of Sin Eaters?<br /> <br /> My gut instinct is to start monsters at potency 2 levels (and make more than one) and see how easily they get stomped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T21:59:09-08:00","id":302979,"title":"","content":"Other Monsters can be useful to add to Geist games to shake things up a bit. I've always used the rules for various games for the monsters myself....Blood and Smoke Vampires are pleanty dangerous for a Sin-Eater, and I use most of the Werewolf Hacks in Armory: Reloaded which makes Werewolves very dangerous. I apply a lot of them to shifters from War Against the Pure, such as the Colony and Brineborn, which makes them pretty dangerous. Demons you can probably bring in as-is as well.<br /> <br /> Unfortunatly, every group of Sin-Eaters will be different. Two of my team are utter badasses, and two have almost no combat ability whatsoever. It really depends on the makeup of your Posse.<br /> <br /> I have never used Dread Powers in a Geist game to make suggestions there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T00:28:54-08:00","id":303049,"title":"","content":"Depends on how you want to &quot;throw them in there&quot;. If its going to be a downright slug-fest, you'll need to either make it so theres an even number of Sin-Eaters and antagonists, or so that the single antagonist vastly over-power a single one of your PC's.<br /> You should also consider what each approach says about the state of your world. If every antagonist the Sin-Eaters meet is an Eldritch monstrocity in his own right, who can crush the individual Sin-Eater with a flick of his hand, then that puts the Sin-Eaters in a position of fear, as everything and their mother can beat them. On the other hand, if everything is weaker than the individual Sin-Eater, then that paints them entirely differently.<br /> By &quot;Demon&quot; I assume you mean the Hunter definition of &quot;Inferno Demon&quot;? If this is true, then I think those can easily be thrown in without any alterations. I strongly suggest the book World of Darkness: Inferno in this case. It has a plethora of awesome stuff for fleshing out demons, ranging from Demonic pacts with Arch-Fiends to Demonically Posessed mortals (Allmost Inferno-Sin-Eaters, actually) and Demon-Ghosts. Those last two I found extreamly flavorful in a Sin-Eater game, myself.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that its practically impossible to permanently kill a Sin-Eater, so it doesn't really brick your scenario if you overshoot the power of the antagonist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}